      *>--- conformance-case
      *> id: g2002_figurative_low_all_symbolic_cd
      *> rules: [2002-GR-8.3.1.2.5.3-6, 2002-GR-8.3.1.2.5.3-8, 2002-GR-8.3.1.2.5.3-9]
      *> accept: [2002]
      *> source-format: fixed
      *> portable: unverified
      *>---
      *> §2002:8.3.1.2.5.3 GR6 - at runtime LOW-VALUE is the character
      *> with the lowest ordinal position in the runtime collating
      *> sequence; "If the context of the figurative constant requires
      *> national characters, the national program collating sequence is
      *> used". By §2002:12.2.5.3 GR9 the program collating sequences
      *> are AL (B first) and NAL (C first), so LOW-VALUE is B in an
      *> alphanumeric context (LX; LCD, a CD record field; LCMP; LCHR,
      *> where FUNCTION CHAR(1) is ordinal 1 of AL) and C in a national
      *> one (LN).
      *> §2002:8.3.1.2.5.3 GR8 - ALL literal-1 is "all or part of the
      *> string generated by successive concatenations of the characters
      *> comprising literal-1", cut to the receiver by GR2b: ABABA,
      *> XYXYX (national), ABCAB for ALL "AB" & "C" (SR2: literal-1 may
      *> be a concatenation expression; §2002:8.8.3.2 SR1 bars an ALL
      *> operand), and in a CD record VALUE (ACD) and MOVE (ACM).
      *> §2002:8.3.1.2.5.3 GR9 - a symbolic-character represents one or
      *> more of its character: STAR and HASH are ordinals 1 and 2 IN SY
      *> (§2002:12.2.6.3 GR11b), * and #; a MOVE fills the receiver
      *> (GR2b: *** and ###), DISPLAY gives one of each (GR2c), and the
      *> CD record legs SCD/SCM.
      *> WHY EACH LEG CAN FAIL: native LOW-VALUE (X"00") or the other
      *> class's sequence in LX/LN/LCD/LCMP/LCHR; a repeat or truncation
      *> error, or ALL bound to "AB" alone (ABABC), in AX..ACM; a native
      *> ordinal instead of the IN alphabet in SA..SCM.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. G2FIG01.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. G2HOST
           PROGRAM COLLATING SEQUENCE FOR ALPHANUMERIC IS AL
                                      FOR NATIONAL IS NAL.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
           ALPHABET AL IS "B" "A" "C"
           ALPHABET NAL FOR NATIONAL IS N"C" N"A" N"B"
           ALPHABET SY IS "*" "#"
           SYMBOLIC CHARACTERS STAR HASH IS 1 2 IN SY.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 W-X3  PIC X(3).
       01 W-N3  PIC N(3).
       01 W-A5  PIC X(5).
       01 W-N5  PIC N(5).
       COMMUNICATION SECTION.
       CD CIN FOR INPUT.
       01 CREC.
          05 F-LOW   PIC X(3).
          05 F-ALL   PIC X(5)  VALUE ALL "AB".
          05 F-SYM   PIC X(3)  VALUE ALL HASH.
          05 FILLER  PIC X(76).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PARA.
           MOVE LOW-VALUE TO W-X3.
           DISPLAY "LX=[" W-X3 "]".
           MOVE LOW-VALUES TO W-N3.
           DISPLAY "LN=[" W-N3 "]".
           MOVE LOW-VALUE TO F-LOW.
           DISPLAY "LCD=[" F-LOW "]".
           IF FUNCTION CHAR(1) = LOW-VALUE
              DISPLAY "LCHR=Y"
           ELSE
              DISPLAY "LCHR=N"
           END-IF.
           MOVE "ABC" TO W-X3.
           IF W-X3(2:1) = LOW-VALUE
              DISPLAY "LCMP=Y"
           ELSE
              DISPLAY "LCMP=N"
           END-IF.
           MOVE ALL "AB" TO W-A5.
           DISPLAY "AX=[" W-A5 "]".
           MOVE ALL N"XY" TO W-N5.
           DISPLAY "AN=[" W-N5 "]".
           MOVE ALL "AB" & "C" TO W-A5.
           DISPLAY "AC=[" W-A5 "]".
           DISPLAY "ACD=[" F-ALL "]".
           MOVE ALL "XY" TO F-ALL.
           DISPLAY "ACM=[" F-ALL "]".
           MOVE ALL STAR TO W-X3.
           DISPLAY "SA=[" W-X3 "]".
           MOVE HASH TO W-X3.
           DISPLAY "SM=[" W-X3 "]".
           DISPLAY "SD=[" STAR HASH "]".
           DISPLAY "SCD=[" F-SYM "]".
           MOVE ALL STAR TO F-SYM.
           DISPLAY "SCM=[" F-SYM "]".
           STOP RUN.
